THE ECHO OF A FISH - (15s · 30fps · High Fidelity)

STYLE & LOOK

Hyper-detailed translucent fish skeleton suspended in a white, soft-gradient void.
Bones behave like glass filaments with refracted red light inside them.
Dust particles drift like slow plankton in the air.
Soft volumetric haze gives a dreamy, weightless aesthetic.
Tone: ethereal, poetic, calm, haunting-beautiful.

GLOBAL MOTION RULES
NO still frames. Skeleton gently drifts and breathes with subtle 1–2 mm flex motions.
Fins ripple like extremely thin membranes catching a slow current.
The entire body rotates very slowly, like suspended in water.
Micro-dust particles float in parallax layers.
Light pulses inside the skeleton follow a soft rhythm, never flashing.
Camera constantly drifts: micro-dolly, micro-pan, slow arcs, macro slides.

SOUND DESIGN
Deep ambient synth pad.
Soft crystalline chimes on camera transitions.
Whispery whoosh with each slow rotation.
Final 0.5s ends on a gentle, resonant glass note.

13-SCENE SCRIPT (≈1.1–1.2s per scene)
Scene 1 (0.0–1.1s) — EXTREME MACRO: EYE SPHERE
Camera inches across the translucent red “eye” cavity. Internal refracted light swirls slowly.

Scene 2 (1.1–2.2s) — SKULL ARCHES
Macro slide under the jaw and cranial ridges. Tiny dust motes drift past like glowing particles.

Scene 3 (2.2–3.3s) — FIRST BREATH
The entire skeleton expands subtly, as if taking a soft “memory breath.”
Fins twitch lightly.

Scene 4 (3.3–4.4s) — SPINE CHORUS
Camera moves along the spine; each vertebra glows faintly, sequentially, like a pulse traveling.

Scene 5 (4.4–5.5s) — RIB CATHEDRAL
Camera reveals the ribs from inside, making them look like a curved cathedral ceiling of glass.

Scene 6 (5.5–6.6s) — SHIMMERING FINS
Close-up of a fin as it waves slowly, refracting red and white like liquid light.

Scene 7 (6.6–7.7s) — FULL BODY ROTATION BEGINS
Camera arcs as the skeleton begins a graceful slow rotation, suspended in the void.

Scene 8 (7.7–8.8s) — MEMORY TRAILS
As the fish rotates, faint ghost-like silhouettes trail behind briefly then fade.

Scene 9 (8.8–9.9s) — SPINE ENERGY FLOW
A soft red glow travels from tail to skull, illuminating the entire structure.

Scene 10 (9.9–11.0s) — EMERGING AURA
A faint translucent outline of a whole fish appears around the skeleton — soft, painterly, ephemeral.

Scene 11 (11.0–12.1s) — CAMERA DIVE THROUGH
Camera flies gently through the rib cage; refracted light blooms softly as it passes.

Scene 12 (12.1–13.2s) — THE RETURN CURRENT
The aura collapses inward, the skeleton drifts back into stillness, glowing softly at its core.

Scene 13 (13.2–15.0s) — DISSOLVE INTO QUIET LIGHT
The skeleton slowly fades into pure white haze as dust particles float.
Last frame holds the dissolving silhouette.

END CARD (clean, poetic):
“Every life leaves an echo.”